  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 311 AM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nCurrently have a broad area of upper ridging spanning from the\nFour Corners region down through the Lower Mississippi Valley.\nAt the surface, a diffuse stationary front extends from\nnorthwest KS into eastern Nebraska. Some scattered showers\ndeveloped a few hours ago in an area of 850-700mb moisture\ntransport that maybe aided by what looks to be an MCV tracking\nalong the KS/NE border.\n\nScattered showers will continue slowly pushing east early this\nmorning and should be exiting central KS by around 12z. With \n850mb temps warmer and 1000-850mb thicknesses greater than \nyesterday, highs today will be similar or even a couple degrees \nwarmer than they were on Monday. This would bring highs in the \n102-106 degree range with heat indices close to or a couple \ndegrees above these temps. There is decent model agreement in \nthe cold front stalling out near or just north of I-70 by Wed \nafternoon. This may provide enough convergence is get a storm or\ntwo do develop after 21z. The bad news is the front will still \nbe too far north to provide any relief from hot temps. \n\nStill looking for shortwave troughing to take place Wed into \nWed night from the Pacific Northwest down into Southern CA. This\nwill deepen lee troughing and increase low level jet Wed night, \naiding in the development of an MCS across Nebraska that will \nlikely last through Thu morning. There is decent agreement now \nbetween most of the models in outflow pushing through most of \nwestern and north central KS on Thu. This may bring some heat \nrelief to parts of central KS along with increased chances for \nshowers and storms, mainly across central KS. Troughing out west\nwill allow a series of monsoonal impulses to lift across the \nRockies and out into the Plains for Thu night through Fri night \nand will result in continued high storm chances from northwest \nKS through Nebraska, especially during the overnight hours. \nUnfortunately, most of this activity will stay north of the \nforecast area. In addition, confidence is increasing that the \nvery hot temps will remain through Fri and possibly into Sat. \nUpper ridging is forecast to push slightly southeast for Sat \nnight into Sun and may allow some slightly cooler air to work \nsouth for the end of the weekend into the start of the work \nweek.",
